// UnitStatEntries (0x2f84b0 -> 0x2fa060 -> D2RCore+0x832940) writes 16 bytes per entry (movups copy, `add r8,0x10`):
// layer, stat, value, and a fourth dword nobody knows (so it is never compared or copied on purpose). A Slot3 dump of a
// map's stat 564 read 00000000 00000234 00000057. The toolkit's older 8-byte note ({u16 layer, u16 stat, i32}) is the
// original body, not D2RCore's.

// D2R's avoid (0x44ef70) sends a walking or running defender straight to the evade roll and never blocks: player modes 2
// (walk) and 3 (run) (plrmode.txt), monster modes 2 (walk) and 0xf (run) (monmode.txt). PD2 blocks with claws in every
// mode (#1483), so the port rolls the class 13 block itself in exactly these modes; in the others D2R's own block runs.

// PD2's no-avoid window (#1482): any avoid (block, evade, dodge, avoid: 0x1e) sets playerdata+0x1c0 = frame + 4, and while
// frame < that the player's avoid roll returns 0 at once (PD2 0x103035f0, players only). D2R has no such field, so the port
// keeps (unit id, until frame) here. A window never reaches more than 4 frames ahead, so an entry further ahead (a new game
// restarted the frame counter) or already passed is stale and its slot is free.

// PD2 Resurrected's own engine values for D2R 3.3.0 build 93847, on top of d2rAI-toolkit's shared/plugin-common (its d2r.h and
// rvas_93847.h hold every shared address, offset and structure: use those, never a copy here). What stays here is a value
// the toolkit does not hold; each entry says why in a line.
// Include this instead of d2r.h. A value another project needs moves to the toolkit's rvas_93847.h, not a copy there.
//
// Every value was found in the Ghidra analysis of the dumped 93847 image; the comment beside each says where (the
// Split Throw spike's FINDINGS.md on branch research/split-throw, or the D2R function it was read from) and the game
// check that uses it. core-rules' names match the RVA column of docs/features/core-rules.md; another plugin's values sit in a
// section headed by that plugin and the work item that found them (core-ui: LP2, #212).

// --- core-ui: HD pictures of 4-character item codes (#310, #298): our patch bytes over the toolkit's ItemsJsonKeyD2R ---
// jmp 0x663a07 / mov [rsp+25],al / movzx eax,word [rsi+2] / test al,al / jne 0x663a10 / mov word [rsp+26],0x2020 /
// jmp 0x663a19 / or ah,0x20 / mov [rsp+26],ax / nop

// --- core-rules: socketed gems and runes apply their mods once (#450; D2Game\src\Items\ItemMode.cpp) -------------------
// 0x475140 (dataFlag, filler, parent item, 0) applies a socketed filler's gems.txt mods; every insert path calls it
// (0x46eb00 and its siblings 0x46e670, 0x46ea70, 0x46e8c0, 0x46ef30, 0x470ca0, 0x4744a0, 0x475090). It takes the mods
// into the filler's own stat list when the filler is a gem (item type row 0x14) or a rune (0x4b), unless that list was
// saved and sent too: the save/packet writer 0x37ffd0 writes the compact form (no stats) when item data +0x18 has bit
// 0x200000 (`flags >> 0x15 & 1`), and the client and the loader then apply the mods once, from gems.txt.
// Our misc.txt has compactsave=0 for every gem (PD2's stacks), so the flag is set here instead. Not in the toolkit yet.

// Property numbers by code (#1371). D2R numbers properties.txt by ROW, skipping the "Expansion" row (the *Id column is only
// a comment), so a plugin that hard-codes a number breaks when the table is edited (#1355). Init reads the mod's
// properties.txt once at load (the way Cartographer's parsePropertyId does); Resolve returns -1 and logs when a code is missing.

// The other Rathma clone (#475, #645): core-events' shared life and core-rules' open wounds both ask for it.
// PD2's test: the victim is a clone, both boss slots (game +0x2600 / +0x2604, kept in D2R's per-game counters under
// rathma_ai.cpp's 'UBR0' / 'UBR1') are set, and the other slot's clone is not dying or dead. PD2 takes the slot whatever
// it holds; the port also wants the other clone's class there, so an id left by Rathma or Mendeln never stands in for it.

// PD2's idle window for a boss left alone (game+0x26fe; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 5): the
// room-release hook (map_open.cpp's KeepBossRoom, PD2 0x102fc6c0) marks a boss whose room has had no player for 10+
// ticks; the boss's next think starts the game's 15-tick window when none runs.

// The Sacrifice Altar's panel (#1192). PD2's altar takes a corrupted amulet through a panel; this is the D2R version,
// built only on SDK services: a 1x1 custom player page (InventoryService) bound to the grid of a left panel
// (PanelService, layout files/data/global/ui/layouts/core-maps/SacrificeAltarhd.json), the buttons caught as UI messages
// (SharedEventService), and the item work as item transactions (ItemService).
//
// Pad focus (#1456): a world open skips D2R's controller steps, so after the open the frame callback repeats what the
// stash panel does when it opens in pad mode (BankPanel open handler, 93847 0x23cc40), by signature, and B closes the
// panel through its own vtable copy (AltarOnMessage). docs/research/controller/altar-world-focus.md.
//
// Flow: the altar's operate (lucion.cpp) opens the panel. Confirm moves the amulet from the page to the inventory, runs
// Desecrate on it there (lucion.cpp; a failed roll makes the brick) and closes every panel. The X and Escape just
// close the panel: a frame watcher returns any amulet left on the page, which also covers a save-and-exit with the
// slot filled.
// shortcut: host only (the SDK names the local player on the UI thread only), as the brick was; a remote use is refused in the log.

// D2R's own pieces of the stash's pad open, found by signature (93847 RVAs for reference only). Any miss leaves the
// panel without pad focus, as before.
// 93847: 0x858050, void (panel): the focus manager takes the open panel

// PD2's cube op 30 (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x365fe0 and 0x366f40; docs/pd2/map-system-dll.md, section 3): when
// an op-30 row's inputs all match the cube's contents, the transmute stops and nothing is made. The row shadows the
// rows after it: the map recipes use it to refuse normal maps (heroic, corrupt, fortify, Catalyst, ears) and unique
// maps (ears), and to stop the generic gem and skull rerolls from duplicating stacked maps.
//
// PD2 checks op-30 rows before its other filters, so difficulty, class, the input count and the stackable check do not
// apply to them; the blocks with a qty input (3 perfect gems, 6 perfect skulls) depend on that, as their numinputs is 2.
// D2R's search applies those filters to every row and has no op 30 (unknown ops pass), so this hook runs D2R's
// search, then walks the op-30 rows up to the row it found (or all of them) through D2R's own input matcher. The first
// op-30 row whose inputs all match turns the result into "no recipe".

// PD2's Dclone AI (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x1035b3f0; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 5) for uberdiablonew:
// the heal when a player leaves, the immunity while his adds live, the three cold-nova phases at the arena centre, the
// three skeleton waves (UberDiabSummon, srvdo 177) and his attack picks. Every other Trap-Melee monster keeps D2R's think.
// The trapped souls' AI (0x1035bc60, monai row 99, #472) is here too: they cast while Dclone lives and die with him.
// That PD2 function's nihlathakMap branch (map boss 0x39a, #538) is in nihlathak_ai.cpp; this file registers it.
//
// Dclone registers on monai row 87 through ai_hooks (no SDK service runs monster AI; see ai_hooks.cpp). PD2 keeps the
// player count in a per-unit map and the last pick in the AI control; Dclone is one per game, so the port keeps both in
// D2R's per-game counters (rva::GameCounter), as lucion_ai.cpp does. PD2 reads the Hell column of every aip, whatever the
// difficulty; so does the port.

struct Grown {
	const char* name;
	uint64_t rva;
	uint64_t extraBytes;
	bool spinLock;  // +0x28 is a spinlock (the Jobs pool), not a lock the engine's lock functions take
	char state[100];
};

// PD2's AI for the Altar of the Catalyst's guardian, GuardianOfFate, and its clone (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x1035a6b0, #609).
// With a target, each think first blinks (Skill1) to a free spot within 8 subtiles when the last think summoned; then
// one roll of 100: under the summon chance, while fewer than 6 summons were cast, the guardian casts Skill3
// (GuardianOfFateSummon, whose missile spawns a clone through core-rules' srvhit 67) on its target, and the chance
// resets; else the chance grows by 6 - summons. Then under 80 Skill2 (Voidbolt) on the target, under 95 a blink, else
// it idles for its aidel. With no target both fall back to their monai row's think, the Regurgitator's (row 71).
// The clones' death with the guardian is map_events.cpp's (AltarGuardianDied).
//
// Both register on monai row 71 through ai_hooks (no SDK service runs monster AI; see ai_hooks.cpp). PD2 keeps the
// blink flag, the summon chance and the summon count in the AI control's three params (1.13c +0x14, +0x18, +0x1c),
// the ones the Regurgitator think keeps its state in; so does the port, at D2R's +0x44 (rva::AiControlParams).

// Horazon, split out of event_portals.cpp (#943). PD2's map event Horazon (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10377ca0): when `summonerMap`
// dies while the game's event is Horazon's, once per game, it drops six native map items rolled from the
// `Cartographer Maps` pool (#959; the PD2 tier pools, map-stat propagation and unique-map roll are gone here).
// The red portal to the second map is Cartographer's cartographer.open-extra.v1 service (#1028, d2r-tools#485).
// The trigger is the SDK's monster-death listener; the TC drop is an engine call, as no SDK service rolls a TC. The
// listener also hands the Altar of the Catalyst's guardian to map_events.cpp.

// PD2's key drop rule (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x103799d0; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 7). On every
// monster death PD2 rolls odds-only TCs: a TC's Unique x max(Set, 1) is a 1-in-N chance, Unique scaled down by the
// player count, and a hit drops the TC's item by the monster. PD2's corrupted-zone rolls (the Talisman and the
// Worldstone Shard) roll in an active Terror Zone instead (docs/deviations.md).
//
// The trigger is the SDK's monster-death listener, which runs on the server thread after D2R's own drop. It hands over
// ids only, so the game, the monster, the Terror Zone test, the TC rows and the drop are engine calls. No SDK service
// covers them from this thread: ItemService creates items for a player handle, not at a dead monster, and
// DataTableService answers Busy off the captured game thread and has no TC lookup by name.

struct KeyRoll {
	uint32_t code;      // items.txt code
	Where where;
	const char* tc[3];  // the TC of each difficulty
};

// Anya's Hell reward (#1323; PD2: ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10372050, docs/research/maps/anya-maps.md). D2R queues Anya's class
// item as a deferred event; its execute function (0x546cc0 in build 93847) makes the item. PD2 also gives, in Hell only,
// 3 random T1 maps (item level 99, normal) in the player's inventory. This runs the original first, then does that.
//
// No SDK service gives an item to a player at a quest step with PD2's drop-to-ground fallback, so the quest item
// function is called as the engine does. All three engine addresses are found by signature at load, never by RVA.

// Map boss loot follows the map tier (#1423). A map boss's superuniques.txt row names one fixed Map Boss TC (T1-T3, and
// the Blood variant in Hell), but the same boss opens maps of every tier, and Cartographer takes at most 16 bosses.txt
// entries (a row per boss and tier would need 23). So the TC is chosen at the drop: D2R's TC drop (rva 0x4404f0, found
// by signature; no SDK service covers it) is wrapped, and when a superunique of a native map drops one of the Map Boss
// T1-T3 classes, the class of the open map's tier (map_events.cpp: MapTier) drops instead, in the same family
// (plain or Blood). Anything else (other monsters, other TCs, no map open) goes through unchanged.

struct Pending {
	bool used;
	uint32_t gameId;     // the game's id (game +0x08)
	uint32_t unitId;     // the Wanderer's unit id
	int32_t due;         // the game frame of the boss
	uint32_t runs;       // game-thread runs without the due frame
	int32_t x, y;        // the spot he left from
	int32_t targetType;  // the target he had at the think's start (-1 none)
	uint32_t targetId;   // its unit id
};

// D2R's think for the Wanderer minus the a3q7 quest gate (see the top of this file). Vanilla: no target or one 20 or
// more away idles; a near target sends him to a spot 20 north of where he is, walks there, and once within 2 of it
// (or after 2 walks back) he leaves. The first `ai control` params (state, walks) live at +0x44 and +0x48, as the
// Regurgitator's do.

// The packets are documented in the d2rAI-toolkit's knowledge/d2r-93847-addresses.md, "Level packets: act darkness (0x53) and level sound (0x2c)".
// PD2 0x1037dc70 (game, act, on): the act's eclipse (1.13c D2Common #10337 on, #10895 off), switched once, and packet
// 0x53 {act, 5, on} to every client in game, as PD2 sends it (D2R's client reads the act as the light period)

// Lucion's death (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10376560; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, sections 5 and 6). When Lucion
// dies PD2 opens a dark grey portal (object 622, the port's 625) at (0x6221, 0x17df) in his arena to the Temple of the
// Triune, with its return portal in the Temple; at tiers 1-2 it drops a Demonic Cube (`imrn`) at 1 in (4 - tier) x 25;
// it sets the fight's stage to 8, which the Temple's altar needs (UB7); and it kills the adds left in the arena
// without drops (Shivering Child, Smouldering Defiler, Anguished Mother and the spawner) and removes his controller.
// It also opens a dark grey portal in Harrogath back into the arena (PD2 0x1038a1f0 at Harrogath's spot 1).
//
// The trigger is the SDK's monster-death listener, as in key_drops.cpp. No SDK service makes a portal, finds a level
// spot, kills a monster or drops an item at a dead monster, so those are engine calls.
// shortcut: the adds are found by class in the arena, where PD2 does it only once the Overseer AI has registered the
// controller (game +0x2604); use that once the phase scripts are ported
// shortcut: PD2 links the Harrogath portal to an `empty` object (587, the port's 590) at the arena's entry spot less
// (5, 5) and removes the waypoints by it (0x1038a510); here the portal's operate (map_open.cpp) warps to the arena's
// entry spot itself and the arena keeps any waypoint. Port the link if PD2's arrival spot ever differs in game.

// UB7b, the brick (PD2 0x103729e0's failure branch): a new rare `amu` at item level 99 replaces the amulet, then
// 0x103649d0 rolls a normal Corruption (flag 0) and the Desecration roll (flag 1) on it. Nothing is read from the old
// amulet. The swap is one SDK item transaction (old amulet in, new one out into the inventory), run on the game thread
// by the altar panel's confirm (altar_panel.cpp). The two rolls are native (editNativeItem): the SDK cannot pick a
// cubemain corruption row.
// The brick is unidentified, as PD2's: 0x1036ebc0 leaves the drop request's force flag and item-flag override at 0.

// UB7a, Desecration (PD2's altar handler 0x103961b0 and roll 0x103729e0; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 8)
// at the Sacrifice Altar's panel (altar_panel.cpp). `item` is a corrupted amulet that is not desecrated or mirrored,
// and Lucion is dead (stage 8): the attempt sets the stage to 9, then succeeds at 50% (60% at tiers 1-2) with one of
// rows 682-689 as desecrate/desecratenum. Native: the SDK cannot add a mod to an existing item. Failed means the roll
// failed and the caller makes the brick (BrickAmulet); Refused changed nothing and says why in the log.

// PD2's Overseer AI (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x1035dca0; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 5) for Lucion (PD2
// 1112), LucionControl (1113) and LucionSpawner (1141): Lucion's stages and state machine, the portal phase, the
// controller's spawner waves and Royal Fire, the spawner's adds. Every other Overseer monster keeps D2R's think.
//
// The three register on monai row 120 through ai_hooks (no SDK service runs monster AI; see ai_hooks.cpp).
//
// PD2 keeps the fight in game fields (stage +0x262a, sub-step +0x262b) and Lucion's AI params; the port keeps them in
// D2R's per-game counters (rva::GameCounter), like map_open's tier. Lucion is one per game, so his params are too.

// The Temple of the Triune's chests (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x103a94b0, read for #438). PD2 wraps the chest operate
// (OperateFn 4): for its LucionChest (object 623) in mode 0 it plays the chest sound, sets mode 1,
// drops LucionChestLow (at most 3 items) and LucionChestHigh (at most 2 + tier: 2, 3 or 4) at the item level of the
// player's area, and opens on event 1 after the open frames. D2R's own chest roll never runs for it. Any other chest
// goes to the original.
//
// No PluginSDK service reports or changes an object's operate, so this wraps the operate table slot (as map_open.cpp
// takes slot 60). The sound, the item level and the TC drop are engine calls.
// shortcut: PD2 also calls a D2Common function on the player first (0x10309650, ordinal 10331, not identified) and
// clears bit 2 of the chest's 1.13c unit flags; D2R's chest is unselectable from mode 1 on anyway. Port both if the
// opened chest ever acts differently from PD2's.

// PD2's map events (ProjectDiablo.dll; docs/pd2/map-system-dll.md, section 4), kept for the native Cartographer
// maps (PD2's own tiered and unique maps are cut, #964). The first room of a native map rolls
// one event for the game (0x10383060): rare and better 34%, magic 17%, normal 11%, always with `map_force_event`
// (a Catalyst Shard); then up to 40 draws of 12, the first naming an event wins (Altar of the Catalyst never when
// forced). The event spawns as the map's rooms activate (0x1036fef0), once the level's progress, rooms activated x
// 100 / PD2's room count for the level, is far enough; it spawns at the activating room's centre.
//
// Shadow of Mendeln, Horazon and Gheed spawn once (Gheed with an event marker object), Dark Wanderer and Treasure Fallen
// up to three times. The Altar of the Catalyst places its altar once: the first use calls its guardian, whose death
// (event_portals.cpp's listener) lets the second use drop 2-3 Catalyst Shards. The Spire of Darkness places its altar
// and three fog objects; once used, the rooms send shadow waves until the progress passes 90, which kills them. Void /
// Tomb opens a portal pair to the Bitter Depths with a marker. The invaders (MS10) place up to three portals; the
// portal's think and the invaders' drops are lane-c/invaders.cpp's. Horazon's death is event_portals.cpp's. The altars' use is PD2's operate 79 (0x103aa460) in D2R's free
// operate slot 35 (pd2_port.FUNCS), which also serves the Temple's Sacrifice Altar (Lucion's Desecration), written into D2R's operate table as map_open.cpp writes slot 60.
//
// Each spawn sends the event's notify string to every player as a red chat line (#336; PD2 0x1037dbc0, packet 0x26
// type 4, colour 1). The SDK's localization service gives the text; no SDK service sends a chat line, so it goes
// through D2R's chat packet sender (rva::SendChat).
//
// No PluginSDK service reports a room activating, so this hooks D2R's room monster spawn (rva::RoomPopulate), the
// function PD2 wraps. The event and the counts live in D2R's per-game counters (rva::GameCounter), so a new game
// starts without them.

// 0x48f190 (game, room): the room's preset loop (pd2_engine.h PresetSpawn), the first of four calls (0x48f190, 0x503790, 0x510f00, RoomPopulate) both RoomPopulate callers
// (the per-frame room loop 0x408670 and the activation 0x4042a0) make for a room that is not active yet (0x2f0600 == 0).
// Decompiled for #950 (Ghidra, D2R.gpr); entry bytes push rbp; push rsi; push r14; mov rbp,rsp.

// Cartographer publishes no room count (event-link RoomProgress), so a native map's progress divides by the room
// count of its built level (RealRooms); NativeTier.rooms (PD2's default 200) serves until it is read.
// For game checks only: PD2R_MAP_ROOMS=<n> in the game's environment replaces the count.

// PD2's 0x1038a060 with unit type 2: an object at x/y, in mode 0 (PD2 passes `type != 2` as the mode: an altar in mode 1
// is not selectable, so no click reaches its operate). No PluginSDK service places objects, so this calls D2R's unit
// spawn (rva::SpawnUnit, argument 8 the mode) as OpenPortalAt (map_open.cpp) does.
// shortcut: PD2 also sets bits 0x3000000 of the 1.13c unit flags (+0xc4), not identified; the altars work without them

// PD2's 0x1036fef0, before the room's own monsters: one roll of 100 per room, against the event's rule. The spot
// search runs from the room's centre with size 12.
// shortcut: PD2 also skips a room its 0x103a2e90 (an engine call through a pointer, not read) refuses, and marks
// Mendeln's monster (+0xd0 = 11); read both if an event spawns where PD2's would not, or Mendeln acts differently

// PD2's operate 79 (0x103aa460) for both event altars, in D2R's operate slot 35. The Spire's first use starts the
// waves. The Catalyst altar's first use calls its guardian 10-29 subtiles off (40 tries, spot size 2), its second,
// once the guardian is dead (AltarGuardianDied), drops 2-3 Catalyst Shards (PD2 at item level 90).
// Each use also plays its sounds to the user's level (0x1037f240); the Spire's darkens the act (0x1037dc70).
// shortcut: the sounds play on each player, where PD2 plays them on the altar (its unit in packet 0x2c): D2R's sound
// sender (rva::SoundPacket) is only known to work for a player; the user stands by the altar
// shortcut: the shards drop by the user, where PD2 drops them by the altar (0x1036ebc0); D2R's drop (rva::DropItemAt)
// is only known to work by a unit that carries a level stat

// A native map's first room: the game has no event yet (Cartographer allows one map per game), so roll it from the map
// item the player used. Cartographer takes the item inside its open call, before the first room activates, and the
// item interaction listener never fired for a right-click (almanac.cpp), so the use-item handler's entry keeps the
// item's quality and forcing marker (0x4f40c0 (game, player, packet): the packet holds the item's id at +10, the same
// message Cartographer's spell 16 answers). Without a map use (a map opened another way) it rolls as a normal map.
// A native map is any item of the Cartographer map type cmap (merge/ids-itemtypes.tsv, docs/cartographer/contracts.md)

// Cartographer hooks RoomPopulate's entry too (its own events) and loads first; the loader's hook engine cannot
// hook one address twice. Hook the call both of RoomPopulate's callers make just before it (rva 0x48f190): its first run
// subscribes to Cartographer's room-populate service, which then gives every room (and the Rathma arena-room skip).

// The map lane's portal operate and the boss-room keep (the uber areas' entry is uber_entry.cpp).
//
// PD2's map opening (item spell 12, moved to D2R's spell 16: a right-click on a PD2 map in Harrogath opened a red portal
// to the level its misc `len` names, with the area rules, stat routing and event roll of the open map) is cut with PD2's
// maps (#964): no PD2 map item is left, and Cartographer owns the item spell dispatchers for the native maps (#945).
// The uber keys open through item spell 19 (uber_entry.cpp's use slot patches), not through this file.
//
// What stays here is PD2's portal operate (77 in PD2, D2R's free operate slot 60 here), which the uber areas' grey portals
// use: each runs the area rules on entry, warps the player in and goes (uber_entry.cpp's UberPortalBegin and Finish).

// PD2 keeps the bits in game +0x2628, which its Tristram opening (0x10383060) sets to 0 after the warp. The port's +0x2628
// ('UBRE') holds the other ubers' entries, so the bits get their own counter: a preset spawned during the opening's warp
// keeps its bit

// Uber Tristram (0xb9), with the game's area 0x29: lesserhydra1 rolls 1 in 20 for each prime not yet placed, in order, and
// lesserhydra2 takes the first one not placed. Returns the prime, 0 when the preset is no placeholder, -1 to drop it.
// shortcut: PD2 also needs the game's area to be Uber Tristram's (game +0x1df4 == 0x29), which the port does not keep.

// PD2's monster spawn hook 0x1038af90 ran the uber tier scaling for every monster spawning in a PD2 level; the map stats it
// also ran are cut (#964). No SDK service reports or changes a spawning monster, so this hooks D2R. Not MonsterSpawned
// (0x494a60): Cartographer hooks it first and the loader cannot hook one address twice (#1032). Its only caller, the
// spawn core 0x493cc0 (params), is free and returns the monster it made (null when it made none, 1 on the 0x49427c path), so the scaling runs
// as the core returns: after the whole spawn, where PD2's hook ran it right after the class setup.

// D2R's champion and unique makers (docs/research/map-events-audit.md section 6), our own signatures; 93847 RVAs are
// for reference only. The waves fall back to plain spawns when one does not resolve.
// 93847: 0x499880, Unit* (game, room, area, classId, mayChampion, x, y, 1, flags): spawn + unique mods + 3-6 minions

// core-events: PD2's map events and uber fights for PD2 Resurrected (maps are Cartographer's): cube op 30, the map events, the
// uber keys' opening and drop rule, tier scaling, AI and drops, Horazon's portal, Lucion's death and the Temple's chests.
// Shared (host and client must match) and NativeHooks; a mod-scoped plugin in <game>\mods\<mod>\d2rloader\plugins (ADR 0004, #1180).
// On a game image other than the one in rvas_*.h it loads, logs the stamp and leaves every part off.
//
// Parts: registered by the lanes (parts.h); each has a one-word name for the log, the status command and core-events-off.txt
// (<game>\mods\<mod>\d2rloader\config\core-events-off.txt), which leaves listed parts out to bisect a crash.

// The Uber Tristram primes summon their minions (UB3, #483). PD2 fights the primes with the plain act-boss AIs and
// writes a wrapper for each into D2Game's AI table (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10361150): Mephisto 0x10357ba0, Diablo
// 0x10357d50, BaalCrab 0x10357f00. Each runs on the AI tick, rolls for one minion near the prime, then calls the
// original think. The same AI rows run the act bosses, so a wrapper acts only for its prime's class.
// No PluginSDK service runs code on a monster's AI tick or spawns a monster, so the wrappers register on the three AI
// rows through ai_hooks.cpp (one table write per row), and the spawn is the engine's, as map_events.cpp does it.

// The Rathma fight's stages outside the AI (docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, sections 5 and 6).
//
// Room activation (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x1036fef0): the first room to activate in each Rathma level sets the stage
// (0 -> 1 in the first level, 2 -> 3 in the second, 4 -> 5 in the third) and spawns that stage's bosses (Mendeln,
// then Rathma, then both clones) at fixed spots, with a ghostly portal that takes the group into the arena (PD2 links
// it to an `empty` marker by the bosses; the port opens none at the start of stage 1, #1262). No room of the arena
// (80 x 80 subtiles about the bosses' spot) spawns its own monsters. It rides map_events' room activation hook: no
// SDK service reports a room activating.
//
// Deaths, on key_drops' monster-death listener (the SDK's): Mendeln (0x10376760) and Rathma (0x103767d0), when killed
// before their retreat, set the stage to 2 or 4 and open a ghostly portal at their spot to the next level. The first
// clone's death (0x10376840) sets stage 6 and the survivor casts RathmaDeath's buff through PD2's helper 0x1036d7d0
// (its AI keeps it on); the second's sets 7, kills the void knights, golems and totem, drops the Tainted Worldstone
// Shard, rolls 1 in (50 - 6 x tier) for an unlimited tome or key and, at tiers 1-2, 1 in 200 for one of three uniques
// (all at item level 130), and opens a gold portal to Harrogath.

// The grey portals' exit (PD2's `empty` marker the three portals at game +0x261c-0x2624 are linked to): level 0 until
// the first move, which is also where they lead before it (the portal's own level, D2R's level entry). Spot (0, 0) is
// the level's arrival, D2R's warp placing the player as PD2's marker spawn does.

// PD2's Summoner AI (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10358510; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 5) for rathmaBone,
// rathmaPoison and their two clones: the life events every 10% (stat 446 the event index, life held at each mark),
// the retreat below 15% through a ghostly portal to the next level, the immunity rules, the stage-6 RathmaDeath buff
// and the attack picks by the aip numbers. Every other Summoner monster keeps D2R's think.
//
// The four register on monai row 53 through ai_hooks (no SDK service runs monster AI; see ai_hooks.cpp). PD2 keeps
// the fight's stage in game +0x262a and each boss's state, sub-step and last state in its AI control (+0x14, +0x18,
// +0x1c); the port keeps them in D2R's per-game counters (rva::GameCounter), the AI's by unit id, as two of a class
// can live at once (one per level). PD2 reads its numbers from the monstats record as one int16 list (aip1, aip1(N),
// aip1(H), aip2, ...) whatever the difficulty, and the Hell aidel; so does the port.

// shortcut: PD2's helper (0x1036d7d0) ORs 8 into the list's flags in expansion games (game+0x10 & 2) and 0x800 for
// a state with states.txt `exp` (D2Common #10226; blank for monfrenzy and disable_tele). D2R's NewStateList's own
// flags stand, as for the uber scaling and map stat lists

// The final pair's shared life (docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 5, read again for #475).
//
// PD2's damage-type step (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10302ca0, in place of 1.13c's 0x6fcfbd00): after the resists, when a
// clone (rathmaBoneClone or rathmaPoisonClone) takes a flagged type and both boss slots (game +0x2600 / +0x2604) are
// set, and the other clone is not in mode 0 or 12, the hit's damage of that type is halved (0x1037c4c0 with 50 / 100;
// the double at 0x1044fc08 is 50.0) and, unless the other has state 8, the other loses that half from its life
// (stat 6, not below 0). Poison (0x103055b0) puts the same poison (rate and length) on the other clone through
// 0x10305460, under the same slot and mode tests and without the state 8 one.
//
// No SDK service reports damage. The step is D2RCore's, called through a slot (rva::DamageTypeStepSlot): the port
// wraps the slot as item_rules.cpp wraps the event dispatcher, and hooks D2R's poison apply inline past its length test.
// The slots are the AI's (rathma_ai.cpp): the unit ids its think keeps per game.

// PD2's uber boss deaths (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10378d80; docs/pd2/uber-bosses-dll.md, section 6). So far
// Diablo Clone's (0x103763d0): Annihilus, and at tiers 1-2 a 1-in-200 roll for one of five uniques; and the
// mini-ubers' organs (0x10377800, 0x10377830, 0x10377860), one each at item level 130. D2R drops the organs from its
// `Uber Izual`, `Uber Andariel` and `Uber Duriel` TCs, which PD2's merged rows replace with items and potions (#484).
// shortcut: PD2's gold portal to Harrogath at the body is left out; a later UB4 slice adds it.
//
// key_drops' monster-death listener calls it on the server thread, and the items drop by the body through D2R's own
// monster drop with the unique row forced (rva::DropItemAt, as key_drops). Native, not the SDK's createItem: its ground
// destination (the only way to put an item at a body) crashed the game a frame after Annihilus appeared, on a null
// room, with exact and automatic placement alike (Slot4, #229). The drop's item level is the monster's level stat, so
// Dclone's (110) is raised to PD2's item level for the drop: at 110, Annihilus (lvl 130) came out magic.

// The uber keys' own item spell (#951): Cartographer owns the item spell dispatchers and the map spell 16, and a key
// that took 16 reached no handler, so the keys (misc pSpell 19 in misc.txt) use D2R's free entry 19
// {check 0, use 0, keep 0}. Both of its handler indexes are slot 0, D2R's `mov al,1; ret` stub in the check table and
// the use table; the slots are written here (no hook), and every other item that reaches slot 0 passes (it did before).

// PD2 0x102fc6c0, on D2Game's room-release check: a room holding a live uber boss is never released, so the boss keeps
// its life between entries and HealBosses finds it. A hook: no SDK service covers room lifetime, and a room mark
// (RoomPortalMark) would stay on the room the boss walks out of.
// The boss is marked alone too: its next think starts PD2's 15-tick idle window (game+0x26fe, ai_hooks.h).

// PD2's uber tier scaling, state `uberscaling` (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10381160, from 0x10371a70; docs/research/
// pd2-uber-bosses-dll.md, section 4). PD2's monster spawn hook runs it after the map stats (0x1038af90) on every
// monster spawning in a PD2 level, so it rides map_stats' spawn hook: no SDK service changes a spawning monster's
// stats. Only the 30 monsters of the uber fights (PD2's set 0x105def0c) are scaled, from the open fight's tier (key
// `UBRT`, PD2 game +0x2629) and entries (`UBRE`, +0x2628), and state `uberscaling` marks them so none is scaled twice.

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch{.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                              .rva = PrimesDrop,
                                              .expected = PrimesDropOrig,
                                              .expectedSize = sizeof(PrimesDropOrig),
                                              .bytes = PrimesDropOff,
                                              .size = sizeof(PrimesDropOff)};

// The Horadric Almanac (IR5, #240), in core-rules since #945. PD2's unlimited Tome of Identify (`rid`) identifies every
// unidentified item on inventory page 0 and in the Cube at once, and leaves the stash, worn and belt items.
//
// Trigger: D2R's own item spell path. A right-click sends the use message, the server's use-item handler 0x4f40c0 runs
// the item's spell entry, and the dispatcher 0x581680 calls the use handler its entry names. Entry 18 (item_rules.cpp)
// names use slot 14, D2R's unused stub, and this file writes that slot of the use handler table. So there is no hook on
// the dispatchers 0x581680 / 0x5817f0, which Cartographer owns beside us (one owner per hook site), and no SDK event (the
// ItemInteractionService raised none for a right-click, Slot4 2026-11-15). It runs on the game thread for any player,
// so a TCP/IP client's use works too.
// PD2's skill 513 handler (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10383ea0) walks the player's inventory list the same way; this identifies
// with D2R's identify (use function 1, 0x57ec30: sets the flag and sends the item to the client).

// PD2's corruption in one press (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x366f40; docs/research/items/ir6-cube-rules.md). A corruption takes two
// rows: a roll row gives the item a hidden `corruptor` value and hands the Worldstone Shard back, then an outcome row
// (op 16 on that value) applies the corruption and takes the shard. PD2 runs the cube again right after a roll row,
// so both fire in one press. D2R runs one row per press; this hook on the executor runs the search and the executor
// once more after a roll row, under PD2's gate (0x364960): the cube holds a Worldstone Shard (`wss ` or `cwss`) and
// none of them is corrupted.
//
// PD2 tags the roll rows with its `ladder` column (2), which the merge cuts. They are the rows whose output carries a
// `corruptnum` mod with a range (1-1000 or 1-3000): exactly PD2's 24 tagged rows, checked against PD2's cubemain.
//
// PD2's Demonic Cube reroll (op 31, 0x3669b0) remakes a unique or set item from its own row and takes one Demonic Cube
// off the stack. On an op-31 row this hook does that through the PluginSDK instead of D2R's executor: one item
// transaction takes one Demonic Cube and the old item and makes the new one in the cube, on the old item's base, row,
// item level, sockets, socketed items, ethereal and identified state, quantity and durability, as PD2 keeps them. D2R's own
// once-per-game rule is skipped (AllowDuplicateUnique), as PD2's 0x103841d0 does. The executor is the hook point only
// because the SDK has no cube event. The SDK refuses item changes inside it (Busy) and names the local player only on
// the UI thread, so the press goes executor -> UI thread (which player) -> next game update (the transaction).
//
// The merge ships the op-31 rows switched off, so D2R never runs them itself; this file switches them on after each
// table load, and only when its hook and the SDK services are in.

// The old item's socketed items move to the new one, as PD2's 0x3669b0 moves them. Native: the SDK's socket policies
// only refuse or destroy them. They come out of the old item before the transaction, so it is an empty input, and go
// into the new item after it, or back into the old one if it fails. The item pointers come from editNativeItem.

// UI thread: the SDK names the local player only here. The pressing player's unit id comes from the executor; a
// native read of the client's own player checks they are the same, since the SDK cannot name the player who pressed.
// shortcut: refuses another player's press in a hosted game (the host has no SDK handle for them without a plugin
// message from their client), upgrade when hosted cube use matters.

// PD2's quiver tiers (#1438): D2R's misc table has no normcode/ubercode/ultracode columns, so the cube's bas/exc/eli tests and
// "useitem,mod,exc|eli" see no tier for a quiver. The items record holds them for every item (normcode +0x84, ubercode +0x88,
// ultracode +0x8c, as weapons and armor); misc rows leave them 0, so this writes PD2's links after each table load.
// Native: the SDK's table views are read-only.

// PD2's stack-aware cube matching (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x364e30, #315). PD2 matches each input with its qty set to 1,
// then takes the quantity (stat 70) of every stack it matched, one per other item, off the input's qty: the input
// matches once nothing is left, so a stack of 3 El runes is 3 El. The row then matches only if every item in the cube
// was used by an input. Its executor (0x3653d0) takes what the row needs off the stacks, so a stack of 5 El leaves 2.
//
// D2R counts each item as one: its search wants numinputs == items in the cube (0x529090) and its matcher (0x529d50)
// counts matching items toward qty. The merge sets numinputs to the sum of the inputs' qty (tools/pd2_items.py). Here:
// - the matcher hook calls D2R's own matcher on a copy of the row with the input's qty out of reach (255), so it flags
//   every cube item that input matches, as it does on a match, and returns PD2's test on their summed quantity;
// - the search's numinputs filter is patched out; the hook does it on input 0 as "no more items than numinputs" (a
//   stack holds several), and on the last input checks that every cube item was used, as PD2 does;
// - D2R's executor takes every cube item whole, so before it runs, the units a row leaves are queued to come back to
//   the cube through the SDK (createItem) once the stack is gone.
// Native: the SDK has no cube-recipe service, and the matcher and search run inside D2R's cube packet handler.

// The forced event goes back as properties.txt map-force-event-l (param = layer, #1371): a SetUnitStat on the made unit
// reached neither the client's tooltip nor the save (Slot3, #1400). Area Level is not passed: map-level adds onto the
// level createItem gives (174, not 87), and a normal map has only that level (the map-level rows take rare maps)

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch {.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                               .rva = CubeNumInputsJump,
                                               .expected = CubeNumInputsJumpOrig,
                                               .expectedSize = sizeof(CubeNumInputsJumpOrig),
                                               .bytes = CubeNumInputsJumpOff,
                                               .size = sizeof(CubeNumInputsJumpOff)};

// PD2's item rules for Ormus' Robes (docs/research/items/p12-ormus-robes.md):
//
// - properties func 25 (`sorc-skill-rand-ctc`, ProjectDiablo.dll 0x103a12a0) in D2R's free property slot 26: one
//   random skill of PD2's sorceress list gets +param, and the item casts that skill on cast (item_skilloncast) at
//   chance min and level max, both adjusted by the skill as PD2 does.
//   The Cast Triggers companion fires item_skilloncast (IR2, the stat's event in itemstatcost.txt).
// - curses (docs/research/items/ir4-curses.md): max curses (a target holds up to the caster's max_curses + 1 curses) and
//   curse resistance (curse_effectiveness on the target scales the curse's stats), around D2R's ApplyCurse; PD2's
//   gate (#264): resisted-to-0 cancels, stat 109 cuts the duration (cap 75 on a player), attract no longer refuses.
//   Dark Pact (#265) consumes a curse and explodes around the target, scaled by the curses it held.
// - skill while equipped and phasing (docs/research/items/ir7-equipped-items.md): item_skillonequip runs its skill as an
//   item aura (D2R's item_aura case and tick, fed stat 375), and Phasing SelfAura drops the unit collision bits.
// - critical and deadly strike (IR3, docs/research/items/ir3-combat-stats.md): PD2's roll and multipliers in place of
//   D2R's, in WeaponDamage's roll block (a byte patch calling WeaponStrike) and D2R's missile roll.
// - op bases, life steal cap and crushing blow (IR3): equipped_eth / missing_hp kept as base stats from the stat
//   callback, lifedrain_percentcap on D2R's add-life, PD2's blow in CrushingBlowApply's jump slot, and its roll on
//   HitEvents' event 5/6 calls, where PD2's open wounds and deep wounds (event 15) run too.

using SetStatFn = int32_t (*)(uint8_t dataFlag, uint32_t a1, uint64_t a2, Unit* item, const void* property, uint8_t set,
                              uint16_t stat, uint16_t layer, uint32_t value, uint32_t a8, uint32_t a9,
                              uint64_t a10) noexcept;

// Called from WeaponDamage's patched roll block (WeaponCritBlock) in place of D2R's: PD2's roll, then the physical
// part (damage +0x18) times 200 + item_crit_multiplier or 150 + item_ds_multiplier percent, each plus the stat's
// per-hand sum (0x103047f0: Javelin and Spear Mastery's crit multiplier sits on the spea layer), flag 0x2000.
// a5 keeps D2R's gate on the mastery's crit (D2R adds it only when a5 is 0).

// WeaponDamage's roll block, found by signature (93847: 0x44c2b4 / 0x44c320 / 0x44c3d9). Cast Triggers byte-checks
// 0x44c2a4..0x44c2b8 (its measurement site), so the head is left stock but for the two bytes at +5: a short jump (EB 65)
// to the stub, which sits over the a5 != 0 path's first 28 bytes (the block's `jne` lands there). Both paths now run
// WeaponStrike (#385).

// D2R keeps an op's result in each stat list's full stats and recomputes it only when a stat of that list changes
// (0x2fa430 walks the changed stat's op targets), so a new op base on the owner leaves a worn item's op value as it
// was at equip time (#320). Moving the op stat by one and back on each worn item that holds it makes the stat code
// recompute its targets with the new base. PD2 needs no such step: it evaluates ops on read (0x102faa90). The op adds
// nothing from the unit's own list (`cheat stat` on the player, seen in game), so only items are walked.
// No SDK service covers stats, so this goes through SetUnitStat rather than a hook in D2RCore's stat engine.

// PD2's 0x102fa640 computes equipped_eth and missing_hp where an op base is read. D2RCore's stat code reads op bases
// itself and never calls D2R's read (0x2f9b10), so core-rules keeps both as the unit's real base stats instead, and
// D2RCore's op 4 reads them: equipped_eth when the unit's summed durability changes (an item worn or taken off:
// itemstatcost.txt gives durability and hitpoints fCallback), missing_hp when life or max life does.
// The server never sends either to the client, so a player's values are mirrored onto its client unit for tooltips.
// PD2's third case, inc_splash_radius + missing_hp x inc_splash_radius_permissinghp (at most 40), is only reached
// with inc_splash_radius as an op base, which no stat has: not ported (docs/research/items/ir3-combat-stats.md).
// shortcut: an ethereal item without durability (a throwing stack) raises no callback; the count follows at the next
// item change. Upgrade with an equip hook if one is found.

// PD2's divisor: 10 on a player or hireling; on a prime evil (monstats flag) 70 + 10 per missing life percent (1.13c's
// D2Common #11027 is the life percent); 8 on others; a monster then adds its player count's life bonus / 50.
// shortcut: PD2's divisor 30 for its own boss lists (0x10371290, built at run time) is not ported; those bosses
// are PD2 content not in the merged data. Upgrade with them.

// PD2's event 16 roll on a hit: item_crushingblow plus its per-hand sum, % 100 on the unit's seed. D2R would roll it
// from the item's event node (itemeventfunc 16), but that node runs D2RCore's own copy of the event table: D2R's blow
// (a quarter of a monster's life, less its damage resist), never D2R's event 16 or CrushingBlowApply's slot (seen in
// game, #446). core-rules hides those nodes from D2RCore's event dispatch for the call (no SDK service reaches it) and
// rolls PD2's blow itself after it.
// Smite rolls its own (skill_functions.cpp, srvdo 150) with calc3 added, so a Smite hit gets no second roll.

// D2R's unit-stat event function (93847: 0x44d570; game, event, attacker, target, damage), which HitEvents (0x44ce80)
// calls for events 5 and 6 and which reaches D2RCore's dispatcher through the 0x5881e0 thunk and its slot. Taken from
// the two call sites' own rel32 (below), not a fixed address.

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch{.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                              .rva = sites[i] - context->exeBase,
                                              .expected = stock[i],
                                              .expectedSize = 5,
                                              .bytes = call[i],
                                              .size = 5};

// D2R's NewStateList (0x433d20, its entry D2RCore's, so not hookable here) refuses a curse at stat 109 >= 100, cuts
// the duration by it uncapped, and refuses a curse on a unit with attract. PD2 does neither, so the call runs with
// the target's stat 109 zeroed on its base layer (the gate already cut `frames`) and its attract bit off. Both come
// back before this returns; nothing else runs in between (one game thread).

// PD2's early-out in 0x1036d7d0, also D2R's NewStateList's first checks (0x433d82-0x433f16): a monster target is
// refused when its monstats row is missing or flagged npc (flags bit 8: byte +0x3d & the bit-mask table's entry 0),
// or its monstats2 row (monstats +0x4c, table +0xf98, 0x128 a row) lacks revive (flags bit 9: byte +5 & entry 1).
// Dark Pact must ask first: its explosion comes before NewStateList.

// --- Replenish charges (IR5) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PD2 (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10345130, 0x103450b0, 0x103451a0) runs item_replenish_charges on the replenish event (3):
// equipping an item with the stat schedules it 2500 / stat + 1 frames on, and each run adds one charge to the item's
// first charged skill below its max (sent to the owner's client) and schedules the next. No SDK service covers unit
// events or charged skills, so both D2R functions are hooked: the scheduler, which every equip calls, and the handler.
// PD2's handler (0x10345320) runs the durability step, else the quantity step, and only when neither added anything
// the charge step, which schedules the next run whatever is pending (D2R frees the firing event only after its handler
// returns, so a pending check there always sees it). The port matches: D2R's step first, then the charges only when
// durability and quantity are unchanged. No merged item has both stats.
// cut: PD2 halves the delay in PD2's PvP maps, cut.

// --- Charm rows (#358) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PD2's inventory is 10x8 and a charm works only in its lower four rows (the grid's y 4 to 7, by the charm's top row).
// D2R's own charm-active body (93847: 0x36ae00) is not called: D2RLoader rewrote its callers to a thunk in its .maho
// section whose `jmp [slot]` reaches D2RCore's charm policy (stock inventory, custom page or both). No SDK service
// covers a cell range in the stock inventory, so the slot is swapped for a wrapper (as for crushing blow), found
// from D2Game's add-to-inventory call site, never by a fixed address.

// Same-name unique charms stored (mode 0, so never the cursor) with their top row in rows 5-8, item excluded; each linked one is
// unlinked (counted in unlinked; pass nullptr to only count, as the draw path must). Returns how many there are, 0 when item is not in the player's item list: the client's remove
// handler 0x1c60a0 asks about the leaving copy after 0x389820 took it out (mode and cell unchanged) and unlinks it and refreshes
// 0x1c9610 only on a yes, so a leaving copy gets D2RCore's answer. A twin D2RCore refuses (unidentified, requirements) still counts.

// The inventory widget's draw (93847: 0x2c3570) asks D2RCore's "requirements met for display" check for each stored
// item (a .maho thunk, its slot swapped like the charm policy's) and draws the item's cell in D2R's red unusable tint
// when it says no. A top-row charm gives no stats, so PD2 tints it red like any inactive item (#1358): the check says
// no for it. The draw is that call's only caller, so no rule sees the answer. The arguments are the call site's
// (item, player, four zero words, the last a dword on the stack), passed on as given.

// Maps (cmap) are never magic (#1415, owner rule #1304): normal, rare or unique. The map TCs lean magic (Map Tier 1-3 Magic 800,
// champion and boss parents 1024) and itemtypes cannot refuse magic, so a magic map is stopped where it is made. D2R's item maker
// (0x442d60) sends quality 4 to the magic affix maker (0x442c60), and the magic fallback of a failed set, rare or unique roll
// ends there too. Refusing for a map (return 0 = "failed") makes the maker fall through to its own superior and normal makers,
// whatever rolled the quality: a forced quality, any call site, or Cartographer's roll hook being absent. Cartographer hooks
// the quality roll and the magic fallback instead (other addresses, so both hooks install); this one is the backstop.
// No PluginSDK service runs inside item creation. The maker is hooked as well, only to log each map's final quality.

// Maps (cmap) stack only when both are normal quality and every stat but the quantity matches, layer by layer (#1326).
// Hooks D2Common's stack-equal check (no SDK service covers it): the drop-onto merge, ground pickup, vendor buys and
// the client's cursor guess all call it.
// D2Common Items.cpp #11102: (target, other) -> 1 when two items may stack; found at load by its signature
// (docs/research/maps/map-stacking.md).

// Progressive Affixes checks the magic affix maker's bytes when it loads and refuses if they changed. Our plugins load
// from the mod folder, core-rules.dll before d2rl-ruffneckk-progressive-affixes.dll (#1180), so this hook waits for
// the first table load, after every plugin's load-time hooks, whatever the load order.
// Runs after ReleaseReserve: its trampoline may take one freed block; 15+ stay for Cast Triggers' 5 relay pages (#1180)

// PD2's item generation and loot rules (IR8, #243):
//
// - the ethereal bonus: PD2's ApplyEthereal (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x102fb710) multiplies by 5/4 where D2R's (0x3d3510)
//   multiplies by 3/2: armor class on a non-weapon; min/max damage, two-handed and missile damage on a weapon.
//   No PluginSDK service sets the factor (ItemService's ethereal edit runs D2R's own 3/2), so D2R's function is
//   replaced at its entry. D2R's callers are kept as they are: the drop (0x442d60), the ethereal property
//   (0x3ccc60) and the cube output (0x5269c0), which calls it with the flag already set. So PD2's early return on an
//   item that is already ethereal is not ported: it would leave cube-made ethereal items with no bonus.
//   D2R's item decoder (0x378860) applies its own 3/2 to a weapon's damage each time it reads one (the client's copy,
//   so the tooltip, and every save load, so the real damage after a relog); those six multiplies are patched to 5/4.
// - an affix's `rare` (#254): PD2's picker (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x10389080, item quality from D2Common #10106) takes
//   0 on no rare, crafted or tempered item, 1 on any, 2 on no crafted or tempered item, 3 on rare items only. D2R's
//   pickers read the column as a flag (0x58c940), so PD2's rare-only affixes (Visceral, the +2 class skill helms, the
//   +3 skill trees) rolled on magic and crafted items. No SDK service filters an affix roll, so D2R's per-affix test
//   (0x3d4220), which both pickers call, is wrapped: it refuses 2 and 3 where PD2 does, then runs D2R's.
// - weapon durability: a weapon's chance to lose durability on a hit is halved (4% -> 2%, 10% -> 5%), as PD2's two
//   bytes over 1.13c's D2Game +0x12f16 / +0x12f36.
// - ethereal durability (#1478): a new ethereal item keeps its base's full maximum durability. D2R's item maker halves
//   the maximum (max / 2 + 1) after ApplyEthereal (0x44350c-0x443553); PD2 turns the `jz` that skips that block on an
//   item with no durability into a `jmp` (one byte, 0x74 -> 0xeb, 1.13c D2Game +0xec4f), so the block never runs.
//   Found by byte signature, patched through the MutationService. See docs/research/items/item-durability.md.
// - throwing quantity (#1489): a throwing stack keeps its quantity when its durability runs out. D2R's weapon durability
//   loss (0x441b10) takes one off the stack (`lea ebx,[rax-1]` at 0x441cb9) before it refills durability; PD2 NOPs the
//   `dec ebp` at 1.13c D2Game +0x13033 in the same branch (+0x12ee0). Found by byte signature, patched through the
//   MutationService.
// - staffmods (#663): PD2's roll of class skills on a new class item (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x1036f470 on disk, 0x1036f400
//   in PD2.gpr) replaces 1.13c's (D2Game +0x13320 and +0x135e0) for every item version: a count from rand%100 + bonus,
//   each skill drawn from a fixed per-class list (knives their own) with a required-level test in place of 1.13c's
//   item-level tiers, and a level from rand%(90 + min(ilvl/3, 10)) + bonus/2. No PluginSDK service runs inside item
//   generation, so D2R's staffmods step (0x58a050) is wrapped: an item of the seven classes gets PD2's roll; a
//   Warlock item (PD2 has no list) keeps D2R's.
// - seal kills (#664): the monsters Chaos Sanctuary's sweep kills when the fifth seal opens drop nothing. PD2 sets
//   their no-treasure-class flag before 1.13c's kill (0x10372e10 over +0xbb4b8). No SDK service runs before a drop
//   (the monster-death event comes after it and only observes), so D2R's mode command (0x4471e0) is wrapped: called
//   from the sweep (its return address), it sets the flag on the monster first.
// Flying monsters' loot needs no port: PD2 patches nothing in 1.13c's drop placement, which, as D2R's (0x444680),
//   puts the item on the nearest free tile by mask 0x3e01, unwalkable tiles excluded.

// The decoder's own 3/2 (0x378860), which client tooltips and every save load use: 3/2 -> 5/4 in place, through the
// SDK's MutationService (no service sets the factor). The new bytes drop cdq's round toward zero: the base damage is
// a weapons.txt byte, never negative.

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch{.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                              .rva = DecodeEtherealDamage[i],
                                              .expected = expected[i],
                                              .expectedSize = 16,
                                              .bytes = bytes[i],
                                              .size = 16};

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch{.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                              .rva = WeaponDurabilityChance[i],
                                              .expected = expected[i],
                                              .expectedSize = 5,
                                              .bytes = bytes[i],
                                              .size = 5};

// Ethereal items keep full maximum durability: the `jz` (74 48) after D2R's "has durability" test in the item maker's
// ethereal block becomes `jmp` (eb 48), as PD2's 0x74 -> 0xeb at 1.13c D2Game +0xec4f. The pattern runs from the test's
// `test eax,eax` through the maximum halving (`sar eax,1; lea r8d,[rax+1]`); the offset points at the `jz`.

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch{.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                              .rva = rva,
                                              .expected = EtherealJz,
                                              .expectedSize = sizeof(EtherealJz),
                                              .bytes = EtherealJmp,
                                              .size = sizeof(EtherealJmp)};

// A throwing stack keeps its quantity when its durability runs out: in D2R's weapon durability loss (0x441b10), the
// stat 70 branch reads the quantity and writes quantity - 1 back (`lea ebx,[rax-1]`, 8d 58 ff); `mov ebx,eax; nop`
// (89 c3 90) writes it unchanged, as PD2's NOP of `dec ebp` does. The pattern runs from the branch's `jle` through
// the stat 0x46 write set-up; the offset points at the `lea`.

const D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequest patch{.structSize = D2RL::Mutations::BytePatchRequestSize,
                                              .rva = rva,
                                              .expected = ThrowingLea,
                                              .expectedSize = sizeof(ThrowingLea),
                                              .bytes = ThrowingMov,
                                              .size = sizeof(ThrowingMov)};

// PD2's lists (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x105de988 in PD2.gpr, filled by its static initializer 0x10191c30), in merged
// skills.txt ids (merge/ids-skills.tsv; PD2's 364-383 moved to 436-455). The Barbarian's has no Blade, Mace or Spear
// Mastery (127, 129, 136); the knives' takes Poison Dagger and twelve Assassin skills.

// Split Throw's return missiles: PD2 missile pSrvHitFunc 65 on the thrown rows, pSrvDoFunc 38 / pCltDoFunc 70 on the
// <name>return rows. D2R fills sdo 38 and cdo 70, so ours sit in sdo 46 / cdo 78 and the data points there.
//
// W6 adds Exploding Arrow's spread (shit 63) and Multiple Shot's pierce falloff (PD2 dmg 17, here 20), both read from
// ProjectDiablo.dll (docs/research/skills/amazon-w6.md).
//
// The server calls missile srvdo as int64_t fn(Game*, Unit* missile) every frame, srvhit as
// int32_t fn(Game*, Unit* missile, Unit* hit) on a collision, srvdmg as void fn(Game*, Unit* missile, Unit* target,
// Damage*) before a hit's damage is applied, and the client missile cltdo as void fn(Unit* missile, float) (the
// toolkit's skill_router.h types).

// dmg 21 (PD2 16, 0x103a6da0): while the missile still has all calc2 bounces (its first hit), raise the physical,
// fire, lightning, magic, cold and poison damage by calc3 percent. PD2's rows have calc3 = par4 = 0, so it adds nothing.
// shortcut: the fire to poison offsets assume 1.13c's +0x10 shift seen on phys and poison length (rvas_93847.h);
// read a D2R srvdmg function that writes them when a row gives calc3 a value.

// dmg 22 (PD2 15, ProjectDiablo.dll 0x103a6c90, Psychic Hammer): each unit the chain hits after the first takes calc2
// percent less magic damage per earlier hit, counted as calc1 (the skill's hits) - the missile's bounces left (D2Common
// #11018, D2R's MissileBounces). D2R's collision (0x4639a0) calls it when srvhit 12 returns 3 (bit 2: deal the damage).

// dmg 20 (PD2 dmg 17, Multiple Shot arrows and bolts): each further unit a piercing missile hits takes DmgCalc1 percent
// less damage, down to dParam1 percent. Scales physical, the elements and the leeches.
// shortcut: PD2 counts pierces in its own pierce hook; this counts hits on the missile's pierce_count stat, so the last
// (not piercing) hit takes one step less than PD2's. Upgrade if the pierce hook is ported.

// shit 62 (PD2 0x103a86d0; Fire Bolt, Ice Bolt, Blizzard, Chilling Armor's bolt): wherever the missile hits, a unit or
// not, every unit within sHitPar1 of the missile takes the missile row's Skill's elemental damage at the missile's
// level + sHitPar2, rolled once, from the owner with PD2's unit mask, the row's HitFlags and ResultFlags | hit. Returns
// 1 as PD2 does, so the collision deals no damage of its own: the struck unit takes the splash.
// shortcut: PD2 also adds the skill's physical damage (1.13c D2Game 0x9f1a0) and puts the missile in the block
// (1.13c +0x5c); none of shit 62's skills has MinDam/MaxDam. Upgrade if a physical row joins shit 62.

// 1.13c's #10573 at sizes 0-2 (D2Common 0x4c570 / 0x4c5c0): the subtile, plus its four neighbours from size 2 on.
// shortcut: size 3 and up test the plus too, where 1.13c tests a wider box; fragments are size 1 (tested at 1 and 2).
// Upgrade when a missile of size 3 or more reaches it.

// --- Summon-on-hit missiles (PD2 pSrvHitFunc 6, here 67; docs/research/skills/w36-monster-kits.md) -------------------------
// Read from ProjectDiablo.dll: shit 6 at 0x103a7750. D2R's own srvhit 6 (0x45ce90) spawns the same monster the same
// way but leaves out the flags, so the spawns would drop loot and give experience.

// dmg 18: besides its own damage, the spear deals a second hit of DmgCalc1 percent of the target's max life, from the
// missile's owner with hit flags 0x1000 (PD2 builds a fresh block and runs 1.13c's hit events 0x10305990 with area 0
// and its result 0x103025b0). PD2 writes the full share to the block's magic (+0x20) and min(share, life) to its total
// (+0x4c): with area 0 the resist step that sums the total never runs, so the target loses the total as it stands, with
// no magic resist. The missile's own block is left as it is.
// D2R native calls: PluginSDK has no damage service, so this calls D2R's HitEvents and DealDamage. PD2 runs no
// crit step here, so D2R's DamageStep (0x5889e0, the monster crit) is not called.
// PD2 also puts the missile in the block (+0x5c): 0x103025b0 reads it only for a kill by skill 96's missile, not this
// one, and D2R's block keeps the hit's x/y there (0x13c, 0x140, read by DealDamage), so the port leaves it out.

// --- Throwing potions (PD2 pSrvHitFunc 60 / pCltHitFunc 65, here 68 / 72; IR5, #240) ----------------------------------
// Read from ProjectDiablo.dll: shit 60 at 0x103a8360, chit 65 at 0x103a6890. The tpot_* potions (and Sharptooth's
// Armageddon, which stays on its stand-in) burst into HitSubMissile1 (the explosion) and a ring of HitSubMissile2 (the
// nova, cloud or bolts).

// PD2 missile functions (missiles.txt pSrvHitFunc / pSrvDoFunc / pCltDoFunc / pSrvDmgFunc): Split Throw's return
// missiles, Exploding Arrow's spread and Multiple Shot's pierce falloff (missile_functions.cpp). skill_functions.cpp
// writes them into their table slots with the skill functions.

// core-rules: PD2's engine rules (skill and hit functions, cube ops, item rules, server hooks) for PD2 Resurrected.
// Shared (host and client must match) and NativeHooks; a mod-scoped plugin in <game>\mods\<mod>\d2rloader\plugins (ADR 0004, #1180).
// On a game image other than the one in rvas_*.h it loads, logs the stamp and leaves every part off.
//
// Parts: each has a one-word name for the log, the status command and core-rules-off.txt
// (<game>\mods\<mod>\d2rloader\config\core-rules-off.txt), which leaves listed parts out to bisect a crash.

// Cast Triggers allocates its 5 relay pages upward from the image (within +0x70000000) when tables load, and D2R's
// render-context init can fill that window first (#1180). Hold the first 16 free 64 KB blocks from plugin load and
// free them in a table listener that runs before Cast Triggers' (mod-folder plugins load in file-name
// order: core-rules.dll before d2rl-ruffneckk-cast-triggers.dll).
// Not a part: the off file cannot drop it.

// PD2's shrine rules in D2R (#1143, docs/research/w37-server-rules.md "Gem shrine"). D2R does none of them:
// - Shared boosters: shrine codes 6-15 run D2R's own effect on the user, then on every other player within a squared
//   distance of 450 of the user (PD2 0x1037d840), through D2R's player iterator.
// - Resist shrines (codes 8-11) add +10 to the matching max resist on the shrine's state list, as PD2 does.
// - Gem shrine (code 18): a stack of gems loses one gem and one upgraded gem is made; D2R's upgrade function replaces
//   the whole stack with the one upgraded gem. The no-gem path (a random chipped gem) is D2R's own. The Perfect Gem
//   Shrine announcement is cut (owner).
//
// How: D2R's shrine function table (16-byte rows: function, stat, state; called as fn(dataFlag, ctx, data) with
// data[0] = the code and ctx = {game, shrine object, user, ...}) takes our wrapper in the slots of those codes, written
// with the SDK's PatchWriteU64 (the almanac's way): no hook for the booster rules. The gem fix needs one inline hook,
// on the upgrade function (game, player, new gem index, old gem unit -> 1 on success), because the loop that picks the
// gem and the code it upgrades to is inside D2R's gem shrine, and the SDK has no shrine event or service. The hook acts
// only while the wrapper of code 18 runs, so no other caller of that function changes.
// Engine addresses are signatures: the three below are ours, the others are d2r::sig entries (resolved by d2r::Bind).
// The part is installed only when every entry resolved. The 93847 addresses in the comments are for reference only.

// PD2 skill functions (skills.txt srvdofunc / cltdofunc / srvstfunc / cltstfunc) in D2R's free table slots, and the
// install of those and of the missile functions (missile_functions.cpp).
//
// The server calls slot `srvdofunc` of rva::SrvDoTable at the cast frame as
//     int64_t fn(Game* game, Unit* caster, int32_t skillId, int32_t skillLevel)   -> non-zero = the skill ran.
// The client calls slot `cltdofunc` of rva::CltDoTable as
//     int32_t fn(Unit* caster, int32_t skillId, int32_t skillLevel)               -> non-zero plays the do sound.
// Start functions (`srvstfunc` in rva::SrvStTable, `cltstfunc` in rva::CltStTable) take the same arguments at the
// start frame; zero refuses the cast. srvdofunc 190 is a router: one slot shared by several PD2 do functions, picked
// by skill id.
// PD2's channel take-over is an inline hook on D2R's mode gate for a busy player (BusyModeGate), which also logs the
// Run/Concentration answers W19's game checks read. Each slot is written with PatchWriteU64 and an expected value of
// eight zero bytes (D2R's own function for the slots it wraps: aura events 32 and 16, srvdo 58), so a slot D2R or
// another plugin already uses is refused and logged, never overwritten. Slots keep PD2's own numbers where free (docs/features/core-rules.md).

// Split Throw (PD2 srvdofunc 189): calc1 missiles of srvmissile a/b/c (by weapon) in Multiple Shot's line, calc2
// activation frame, calc3 triggering missiles. PD2's calc1 is par1+min(lvl/5,par2).
// shortcut: calc4 (PD2's ED%) is not applied; Multiple Shot takes its calc4 through create callback 4 instead (#1056).
// Upgrade when PD2's srvdo 189 is read from ProjectDiablo.dll.

// Multiple Shot (PD2 srvdofunc 8, #1056): Split Throw's line with PD2's rules. calc1 missiles, calc2 activation frame,
// calc3 triggering missiles (at most calc1; 0 = none, so Multiple Shot Proc's arrows trigger nothing). calc4 is the
// missiles' damage % (stat 25). D2R's srvdo 8 reads calc5 for that, so calc4 rides on create callback 4 instead.

// PD2 srvdo 154 (ProjectDiablo.dll 0x103b1590): one missile of srvmissile a/b/c by the weapon, thrown the way D2R's
// Double Throw throws (srvdo 74's 0x4333f0), with damagepercent = calc1 and calc2 bounces (missiles.txt pSrvHitFunc 30
// -> 66 spends them). A monster (UberMadawcDoubleThrow, the same missile in all three columns) throws column a.

// Bash (PD2 srvdofunc 158): a hit knocks back half the time (PD2's Bash row has no ResultFlags). The queued hit's
// knockback bit is set from the roll, then D2R's melee do function applies it.
// shortcut: PD2 rolls after the first apply and only for targets with flag 0x8000; this rolls before, for every
// target. Upgrade if knockback on bosses differs from PD2 in play.

// PD2's teleport core: refused under disable_tele, else D2R's Teleport (srvdo 27), which
// makes the core's level checks (levels.txt Teleport 0 refuses, 2 checks collision at the point).
// PD2's Hell-only level list (0x105de86c) is never filled, so it is left out.
// shortcut: PD2's "TeleportBlocked" chat line on a Teleport 0 refusal is left out: no ported level has Teleport 0.
// Upgrade when one does.

// PD2 srvdo 155: the core, then a ring of calc2 srvmissilea at the new point (LucionBlink's nova), then aurastate
// (teleportdebuff) for auralencalc frames with each mastery lowered by Param2 - calc1 (TeleportDebuff). Named Pd2
// because rva::SrvDoTeleport is D2R's slot number.
// shortcut: an extended list's new timer is not sent to the client (PD2 sends packet 0x83), as for Blood Warp.
// Upgrade if the client's debuff runs out early in play.

// --- Blood Warp (PD2 srvdofunc 157 -> router 190, srvstfunc 66 -> 80, cltstfunc 56 -> 63) --------------------------
// Read from ProjectDiablo.dll: srvdo 157 at 0x103b1aa0, srvst 66 at 0x103b6460, cltst 56 at 0x103acda0
// (docs/research/skills/w12-blood-warp.md). The cast costs life and never kills; the cost comes back as hpregen.

// PD2 srvdofunc 157: teleport, then pay the cost (checked again at the new point) and get it back over auralencalc
// frames as aurastat1 (hpregen) = cost / frames + 1 on an aurastate (bloodwarp) list. A recast at the same level
// extends the running list and keeps its regen; a lower level pays and adds none (TimedStatList).
// shortcut: an extended list's new timer is not sent to the client (PD2 sends packet 0x83). Upgrade if the client's
// state runs out early in play.

// --- Melee splash (PD2 srvdofunc 163 -> router 190) ---------------------------------------------------------------
// Read from ProjectDiablo.dll: srvdo 163 at 0x103b2340, its per-unit callback 0x10303190; Revive's aura event 32
// (0x10347370) calls the do function itself (docs/research/skills/w33-melee-splash.md). Every unit within calc3 of the struck
// unit, the struck unit aside, takes a hit with no to-hit roll: a player's current skill's damage (W35) and the
// attacker's weapon damage at that skill's SrcDam, with half the life leech, through D2R's area search with PD2's unit
// mask. The radius is calc3 + the inc_splash_radius held by the weapon's item types / 20, 1 less on a normal-tier base.
// shortcut: Smite's splash takes Smite's skill damage, not its shield damage and state 224 list (0x103060c0), and the
// radius counts only the weapon's own item types, not PD2's off-hand rules for 1han / 2han (0x10381720); upgrade with
// the deviation row. PD2's room check (0x1037c820) refuses only PD2's PvP maps, cut.

// One unit in range (PD2's callback 0x10303190): a hit with no to-hit roll and the current skill's flags, damage% and
// hit class, the skill's elemental and physical damage, weapon damage at SrcDam, life leech halved (at least 1). Counts
// the units the hit lands on.
